xnu 0281: say how many frames each display tick was given

`present` reads 49-57/s while the renderer asks for 60 (`fps 59-62`) during a
drag (ring246, the horizontal sweep of `0280`). With one pending record per
tick, a tick that finds none holds the previous frame for two periods, and a
tick that finds two can present only the newer. Both show as the same stutter
and both are invisible in a per-second rate.

The tick now counts the records it was handed (0, 1, 2, 3+) and the last eight
intervals between records are printed in microseconds, so one boot separates a
renderer that is late (records arrive after the tick) from one that is bursty
(two records, then none).

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -320,6 +320,10 @@
 	uint32_t      fPresentCount;     /* frames put on the panel */
 	uint64_t      fPresentTicks;
 	uint64_t      fPresentMaxTicks;
+	uint32_t      fTickSwaps;        /* fSwapCount at the last tick */
+	uint32_t      fTickRec[4];       /* ticks that saw 0, 1, 2, 3+ records */
+	uint32_t      fSwapGapUs[8];     /* the last eight gaps between records */
+	uint32_t      fSwapGapIndex;
 
 	bool start(IOService *provider) APPLE_KEXT_OVERRIDE;
 	void addClient(IOMobileFramebufferUserClient *client);
@@ -605,6 +609,17 @@
 	if (fb->fDeferPresent) {
 		uint8_t rec[MONDRIAN_FB_SWAP_REC_SIZE];
 		bool have;
+		uint32_t got = fb->fSwapCount - fb->fTickSwaps;
+
+		/*
+		 * A tick that finds nothing cannot present, and a tick that finds two
+		 * can only present the newer: the panel then holds one frame for two
+		 * periods and moves twice in the next. How many records each tick
+		 * brings is the difference between a renderer that is late and one
+		 * that is bursty, and the two need opposite fixes.
+		 */
+		fb->fTickSwaps = fb->fSwapCount;
+		fb->fTickRec[got < 3 ? got : 3]++;
 
 		IOLockLock(fb->fLock);
 		have = fb->fPendingValid;
@@ -743,6 +758,11 @@
